WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:02.740
Most data tools make you choose:

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.060
drag boxes, or write code.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.980
Duckpad gives you both.

00:00:07.060 --> 00:00:09.700
Duckpad is a free, open-source workspace for

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:12.620
data pipelines, powered by DuckDB.

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:14.740
Connect steps on a canvas:

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.500
load, join, filter, aggregate, export.

00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.700
Every step is a SQL query or a Python class

00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:23.300
you can read and edit.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:25.700
Open the code beside the canvas, and preview

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:27.940
it on real rows as you type.

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.420
Every step keeps its result, so you never

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:32.580
have to guess what the pipeline did.

00:00:32.660 --> 00:00:33.700
Missing a step?

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.500
Write your own.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:36.820
A few comments declare its inputs,

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.260
parameters, outputs and tests.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:42.140
Duckpad turns them into ports, a form and a

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.180
palette entry.

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.940
Nothing to compile, nothing to register.

00:00:46.180 --> 00:00:49.300
Data tests sit next to the SQL they check:

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:51.380
bad rows stop the result before it is

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.220
exported, and they are one click away.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.100
Click any number to see how it was

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:58.820
calculated, through joins and aggregates,

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:00.660
down to the source cells behind it.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.700
Before you rename a column, see every step

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:04.740
it reaches.

00:01:04.820 --> 00:01:07.300
And when a step cannot be explained, Duckpad

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.340
says so.

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:11.300
Every save is a Git commit, and every run is

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:12.340
recorded.

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.580
Run the approved version from the interface,

00:01:14.660 --> 00:01:16.900
the command line or your scheduler.

00:01:16.940 --> 00:01:18.580
Duckpad even writes your project's

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.700
documentation, ready to export as a PDF.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:23.060
Need a hand?

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:25.700
The AI assistant explains a flow and makes

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.100
edits you can undo, with the provider of

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:30.300
your choice, even a local model.

00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:33.780
No cloud, no sign-up, no paid edition.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:35.820
Two commands, and you are in.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:36.740
Duckpad.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:38.020
See the flow.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:39.620
Trust the result.
